{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And the men whom Moses sent.</b> Who had been loyal to him and became his enemies." "<b>And they spread an evil report and caused the whole congregation to murmur.</b> That is, the Sanhedrin and the heads of the people, when they said: כִּי חָזָק הוּא מִמֶּנּוּ (Numbers 13:31). This they did in order to spread an evil report about the land — so that while the elders were occupied with their own murmuring, they could spread an evil report about the land to the masses. This they could not have done in the presence of the elders, who knew and recognized their falsehood."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:54.972968502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}